# J17 — Canonical five-phase cockpit reference
# Governing reference: <operator-reference>/Kuzushi TUI.pdf
# SHA-256: fad7e9bc324572ccf3e03b2e5c71878d1a6eba2795493f4a12005f0178a6f545
#
# The explicit DevEx hook enriches only the canonical offline-demo target with
# the same deterministic state used by the buffer contract. It cannot write
# into an operator target. The picker's `d` key hook was retired; the current
# product enters the offline fixture with the `:demo` command at the target
# gate (the picker hint says exactly that). Entered via `submit:` — not blind
# type+Enter — because async picker hydration can corrupt an in-flight draft
# (the known "scanj"/"demoj" corruption; submit verifies the draft renders
# intact and retypes it if corrupted).
# Numeric page keys are printable view hotkeys, so this journey converges
# Navigate mode (nav-mode: polls the footer markers; F2 is retired) before
# selecting Map, Scan, and Review. The Workbench binds a digit only for those
# three pages; Prove and Fix are compatibility readers reached by their phase
# verbs, so this journey submits `prove` and `fix` instead of 4 and 5.
name: Canonical five-phase cockpit reference
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME COLORTERM=truecolor KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_DEVEX_PHASE_FIXTURE=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
submit: demo
wait-for: 120 PDF phase reference fixture loaded
keys: Escape
submit: workbench
wait: 2
nav-mode:
keys: 1
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Map | 1-map
expect-ansi-profile: truecolor
expect: PROJECT CONTEXT
expect: ATTACK SURFACE
expect: HOT MODULES
expect: DATA-FLOW MAP
expect: NEXT
ask: Map — does project readiness lead, with real attack-surface and threat-model context supporting one obvious NEXT action?
keys: 2
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Scan | 2-scan
expect: SCOPE / PLAN
expect: RECORDED ENGINE OUTCOMES
expect: recorded tool sast:scan
expect: SCAN RECEIPT
expect: outcome completed
ask: Scan — do accepted attempts, engine outcomes, deltas, and the recorded receipt remain distinct from live Run Focus progress?
keys: 3
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Review | 3-review
expect: FINDINGS
expect: SELECTED FINDING
expect: F-0001
expect: SQL injection reaches query
expect: runtime_verified
ask: Review — is the queue confidence-first, is exactly one selected identity obvious, and do actions visibly target that finding?
submit: prove
wait-live-snap: 10 Viewing Prove | 4-prove
expect: STATUS / NEXT
expect: SQL injection reaches query
expect: EVIDENCE
expect: PROOF · REPLAY
expect: replay verify-phase
expect: verify F-0001
ask: Prove — do identity, STATUS, and NEXT precede evidence, with replay offered only for the persisted verification run?
submit: fix
# Remediation truth hydrates async — wait on the loaded lifecycle state
# ("Staged for approval", seeded by the fixture), not merely the page chrome.
wait-live-snap: 15 Staged for approval | 5-fix
expect: Viewing Fix
expect: BREAKDOWN REPORT
expect: VERIFICATION
expect: DFD
expect: REMEDIATION
expect: report
ask: Fix — does remediation lifecycle lead the operator toward an authorized next action while diagrams remain supporting evidence?
keys: Escape
